    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12079" root="دبو and دبى" body-key="d">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ادبى</span></b> , said of the [tree, or shrub, called]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِمْث</span>, (S,) or of the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَرْفَج</span>, (M, K,) or of each of
these, (TA,) <i>It put forth what resembled</i> [<i>the
young locusts termed</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبًى</span>; (M, K;) [i. e.] <i>what
came forth, of its leaves, resembled</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبًى</span>; (S;)
<i>and thus became fit to be eaten.</i> (S, M.) [See
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْقَلَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَقَّبَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَطَ</span>; and see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِمْثٌ</span>, and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَرْفَجٌ</span>.]

